      "inspected_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor": "DESCRIPTION declares R>=3.5.0, Rcpp linking, listed imports and GPL-3 at the selected commit; NEWS and check workflow document maintenance intentions, not passing runs.",
          "inspection": "Pinned primary code, documentation or test specification"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The selected feols documentation describes recursive singleton/perfect-fit removal and observation/collinearity diagnostics; finite negative weights error, zero weights are removed and missing weights join sample selection.",
          "inspection": "Pinned primary code, documentation or test specification"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The selected covariance path reads session defaults; onLoad sets all covariance defaults to iid. Fixed-effect syntax therefore does not itself specify clustered errors.",
          "inspection": "Pinned primary code, documentation or test specification"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "ssc separates K and G scaling from t degrees of freedom, with none/full/nonnested FE counting and optional exact counting. Upstream tests specify irregular-FE examples but were not run here.",
          "inspection": "Pinned primary code, documentation or test specification"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "vcov_fix defaults TRUE. The inspected executable branch assigns a repaired covariance only inside if(vcov_fix); its adjacent always-fix comment is inconsistent. The warning threshold is 1e-8.",
          "inspection": "Pinned primary code, documentation or test specification"
        },
        {
